Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `channelGrouping`: traffic acquisition dimension that we need to group by.  
• `geoNetwork_country`: country of the visitor; used to find the top‑performing country inside each channel.  
• `totals_transactions`: number of transactions in the row; will be summed to get the totals.  
• `visitId`, `fullVisitorId`, `hits_time`, `hits_transaction_transactionId` (not always populated): can be used in a de‑duplication step (e.g. choosing `DISTINCT` on these keys).

Typical conditions / filters that might be used  
• `totals_transactions IS NOT NULL` – keep rows that actually contain transaction counts.  
• De‑duplicate by using a sub‑query with `SELECT DISTINCT` (or grouping on identifying keys).  
• `HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT geoNetwork_country) > 1` – keep only channels present in more than one country.  
• A window function (`ROW_NUMBER` / `RANK`) partitioned by `channelGrouping` ordered by summed transactions DESC to pick the top country per channel.

Ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries
```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at 20 raw rows from rev_transactions
SELECT *
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List of distinct channel groupings in the dataset
SELECT DISTINCT channelGrouping
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List of distinct countries that have at least one transaction record
SELECT DISTINCT geoNetwork_country
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
WHERE totals_transactions IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Distinct combination of channel and country (after de‑dupe)
SELECT DISTINCT channelGrouping, geoNetwork_country
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
WHERE totals_transactions IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
